Previous HEAD position was 5911de40 chore(release): v0.75.0 — resilience wave. README: release prose to v0.75.0 (B=1 parity +4.4%, host-bounce fallback, shutdown join); Recent fixes gains eagerpar receipt, hostbounce receipt with the byte-probe doctrine, ringval 2->12 capacity number, shutdown-join line. Workspace 0.74.0 -> 0.75.0 (internal pins bumped).
HEAD is now at c58ebd62 Merge lane/cx-27btune: 27B NVFP4 decode tune from the ncu anatomy — dual-launch fusion of the 48 linear-attention layers' tiny ssm_beta/ssm_alpha NVFP4 projections (96 grid-12 launches/round -> 48 dual grid=(12,2) launches; same warp template body + reduction order). Naked K=3 spec decode: N=5 interleaved one-lock median 95.98 -> 97.08 tok/s = +1.15%, every paired rep positive, identical tokens/acceptance/rounds across all 10 runs. New kernel-check cell DUAL-BATCHED-AUX pins 48-row bit identity; run-gen MATCH; run-spec 8/8. MEMRA_NVFP4_AUX_DUAL=0 rollback seam. Rejected + deleted per lane law (rows in arms.jsonl, raw retained): eight-resident rpr2w8 async refill (+17.6/+22.7% latency m=3/4), four-way scalar FA partition (-3.34%, fold order changed). The DRAM-bound dual_b4_rpr2 carrier (86.8% DRAM) deliberately untouched — no reuse/layout mechanism found, prefetch-only arms refuted twice. Board unchanged (no published numbers moved). Vast pre-release battery still required before any tag per RESULTS.
